cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the archived release (this file)
  and the manuscript / preprint listed under preferred-citation.
type: software
title: >-
  Python Scripts and Results for "Antarctic Sea-Ice Freeboard from Envisat
  and CryoSat-2: Attributing Inter-Product Spread to Snow and Radar-Retrieval
  Contributions"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-05-28"
license: MIT
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/xinlongliu0307/antarctic-winter-freeboard-comparison
url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19977864
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19977864
abstract: >-
  Processing and figure-generation code, together with selected derived
  outputs, used to intercompare Antarctic winter sea-ice freeboard products
  from Envisat and CryoSat-2 (ESA CCI, LEGOS, CryoSat+ Antarctic Ocean, and
  Cryo-TEMPO) on the Climate Change Initiative 50 km EASE2 grid. The
  workflow regrids, masks, sector-averages, and harmonises the products
  with respect to a common snow reference, and attributes the inter-product
  spread to snow assumptions and radar-retrieval contributions.

